{
 "_comment": "Creature art from bg3.wiki for the Bestiary/Codex creature plates (EPIC D). Each entry maps a bg3.wiki creature page -> creature:<slug> where <slug> is the live bestiary creature name slugged exactly as screen-bestiary.jsx derives it (toLowerCase, [^a-z0-9]+ -> '-', trimmed). The viewer's _scope_key normalises 'creature:<slug>' and the UI's 'creature-<slug>' to the SAME key ('creature' is NOT a stripped prefix), so ingested art resolves. SUFFIXED 2024-SRD names map to the matching bg3.wiki bare-name page (Goblin -> goblin-warrior/boss/minion; Bugbear -> bugbear-warrior/stalker; Bear -> black/brown/polar). A few canon pages stand in for a family (Red Dragon -> the red chromatic line). Official wiki images are (c) Larian -> land ONLY in gitignored content/worlds/_private/<world>/images/, never committed. Re-run: python3 tools/ingest/wiki_images.py tools/ingest/manifest_images_creatures.json",
 "world_id": "baldurs-gate",
 "rate_delay_seconds": 0.4,
